# M16: what the file dialog says when it cannot do what it was asked: a name that is not there, a name DOS keeps for a device, a name that is
# not valid and a path that is too long. The drive that is not ready is `m16-errors-drive`, which only the host can play.
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\A1234567\B1234567\C1234567\D1234567\E1234567\F1234567\G1234567\H1234567
@dir A1234567\B1234567\C1234567\D1234567\E1234567\F1234567\G1234567\H1234567
f10 down enter                # File > Open...
x period q enter              # X.Q is not there
enter                         # OK
altn bspace bspace bspace
l p t 1 enter                 # LPT1 is a device
enter
altn bspace bspace bspace bspace
x pipe enter                  # a name with a bar in it
enter
altn bspace bspace
a b c d e f g h period q l d enter   # C:\A1234567\...\H1234567\ABCDEFGH.QLD is 84 bytes
enter
esc                           # leaves the dialog
